    of the gradient at zero even for higher-order derivatives:

    >>> f = jnp.sinc
    >>> for i in range(1, 6):
    ...   f = jax.grad(f)
    ...   print(f"(d/dx)^{i} f(0.0) = {f(0.0):.2f}")
    ...
    (d/dx)^1 f(0.0) = 0.00
    (d/dx)^2 f(0.0) = -3.29
    (d/dx)^3 f(0.0) = 0.00
